        <TopPick />

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. How to Waterproof Cinder Block Walls: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            The best way to seal cinder blocks to avoid moisture is to work in order: find out what kind of water you have, fix the outside water sources, clean and patch the block, then apply the one product family that suits the wall. Interior basement block that seeps gets a cement-and-latex masonry waterproofer brushed hard into bare block. Above-grade exterior, garage and garden walls get an invisible silane-siloxane repellent. The steps below take most homeowners two or three weekends, largely because of drying time.
          </p>

